-- Chapter: Genesis 35 — BETHEL REVISITED, THE VOW KEPT, THE NAME REAFFIRMED, THE COVENANT RENEWED: Elohim calls Jacob back to Beth-el — "Arise, go up to Beth-el, and dwell there: and make there an altar"; Jacob purges his household — "Put away the strange gods that are among you, and be clean, and change your garments" — and buries the teraphim and earrings under the oak by Shechem; he builds the altar and calls it El-beth-el, the vow of Genesis 28 kept; Elohim appears again and seals the wrestling-name — "thy name shall not be called any more Jacob, but Yashar'el (Israel) shall be thy name"; the Abrahamic covenant renewed — "I am El Shaddai (God Almighty): be fruitful and multiply; a nation and a company of nations shall be of thee... and the land which I gave Abraham and Isaac, to thee I will give it"; Rachel dies bearing Benjamin (Ben-oni → Benjamin) and is buried on the way to Ephrath/Beth-lehem; the twelve sons numbered; Isaac dies and Esau and Jacob bury him.
-- Tag: ge35   Temp view: _s301_ge35_lookup
