--   ★★ v.11-12 (I am El Shaddai: be fruitful and multiply; a nation and a company of nations shall be of thee, and kings shall come out of thy loins; and the land... to thee I will give it, and to thy seed)
--        NT:     none warranted distinct (the company-of-nations regathering is carried by the Tanakh two-house prophets; no NT member added without forcing — the gathering forward-weave is held in the thread prose)
--        Extras: Jubilees 32:18-19 (I am Yahuah who created the heaven and the earth, and I shall increase you and multiply you exceedingly, and kings will come forth from you... I shall give to your seed all the earth) — THREAD 4
--        Tanakh: ★ Genesis 17:1-6 (I am the El Shaddai... I will make thee exceeding fruitful, and I will make nations of thee, and kings shall come out of thee) — the SAME El-Shaddai covenant first to Abraham; ★ Genesis 48:19 (his seed shall become a multitude of nations) — the company/multitude of nations = Ephraim; ★★ Ezekiel 37:19 (the stick of Joseph... and the stick of Yahudah, and make them one stick); Ezekiel 37:22 (they shall be no more two nations); Jeremiah 31:10 (He that scattered Yashar'el will gather him) — THREAD 4 (the two-house seed weave)
--   ★ v.16-20 (a little way to Ephrath: Rachel travailed... Ben-oni → Benjamin; Rachel died, buried in the way to Ephrath, which is Beth-lehem; Jacob set a pillar)
--        NT:     ★ Matthew 2:18 (In Rama was there a voice heard... Rachel weeping for her children... because they are not) — THREAD 5 (the Bethlehem/weeping-Rachel forward-weave)
--        Extras: Jubilees 32:33-34 (Rachel bare a son... called his name "Son of my sorrow"... but his father called his name Benjamin... Rachel died there and she was buried in the land of Ephrath, the same is Bethlehem); Jasher 36:10-12 (Rachel bare a son and she had hard labor and she died... buried her in the way to Ephrath, which is Bethlehem... called the name of his son... Benjamin) — THREAD 5
--        Tanakh: ★ Micah 5:2 (thou, Beth-lehem Ephratah... out of thee shall he come forth... ruler in Yashar'el); ★ Jeremiah 31:15 (A voice was heard in Ramah... Rahel weeping for her children) — THREAD 5
--   ★ v.22-26 (Reuben defiled his father's bed; the twelve sons numbered; the houses of Leah, Rachel, Bilhah, Zilpah)
--        NT:     none warranted distinct (the twelve-tribe structure is carried by the Tanakh laterals and the extras; no NT member without forcing)
--        Extras: ★ Jasher 36:15 (the birthright was given to Joseph, the kingly office to Judah, and the priesthood to Levi, because Reuben had defiled his father's bed); Jubilees 31:13 (Isaac blesses Levi — to approach Him to serve in His sanctuary), Jubilees 31:18 (to Yahudah... In you be found the salvation of Yashar'el) — THREAD 6
--        Tanakh: none warranted distinct beyond THREAD 6 (the sceptre-of-Judah/priesthood weave is carried by the extras here; Gen 49 belongs to its own pack)
--   v.5-6 (the terror of Elohim on the cities; Jacob came to Luz/Beth-el) — folded into THREAD 2 prose (the safe journey to the kept vow); no distinct member.
--   v.8 (Deborah Rebekah's nurse died, buried under an oak, Allon-bachuth) — narrative notice; Jubilees 32:30 / Jasher 36:4 parallel it but it is not framework-load-bearing; NOT forced as a member.
--   v.13-15 (Elohim went up; Jacob set up a pillar of stone, poured a drink offering and oil; called the place Beth-el) — the pillar/anointing echoes Gen 28:18; folded into THREAD 2 prose; no distinct member.
--   v.21 (Yashar'el spread his tent beyond the tower of Edar) — narrative notice; no add.
--   v.27-29 (Jacob came to Isaac at Mamre/Hebron; Isaac died, old and full of days; Esau and Jacob buried him) — NO ADD: a closing patriarch-death notice. Jasher 36 lacks Isaac's death here (places it later); Jubilees has it in ch36. The reconciliation of Esau and Jacob at the grave is a narrative coda, not bound to a framework verse-type in this pack.
