--   5. genesis-35-rachel-buried-on-the-way-to-bethlehem — NT (Matthew) + Tanakh (Micah, Jeremiah) + Extras (Jubilees, Jasher) [extras] (★ Ben-oni/Benjamin; Ephrath/Bethlehem; weeping Rachel)
--   6. genesis-35-the-twelve-sons-the-sceptre-and-the-priesthood — Extras (Jasher, Jubilees) [extras] (★ birthright to Joseph, kingship to Judah, priesthood to Levi)
--
-- Framing notes:
--   ★ PUT AWAY THE STRANGE GODS (THREAD 1): *Put away the strange gods that are among you, and be clean, and change your garments* (35:2). The teraphim Rachel stole — *Rachel had stolen the images that were her father's* (Gen 31:19) — and the earrings are buried under the oak by Shechem. The NT call is the same purge: *let us cleanse ourselves from all filthiness of the flesh and spirit* (2 Cor 7:1), *come out from among them, and be ye separate... touch not the unclean thing* (2 Cor 6:17), *keep yourselves from idols* (1 John 5:21) — covenant separation, never a new ethic; the household made clean to go up to the altar. Read through Red Lines #3/#6: holiness IS covenant-keeping.
--   ★ THE VOW KEPT (THREAD 2): *Arise, go up to Beth-el, and dwell there: and make there an altar* (35:1). The vow of *If Elohim will be with me... then shall Yahuah be my Elohim... this stone... shall be Elohim's house* (Gen 28:20-22) is now PAID — El-beth-el, the God of Beth-el. The pillar poured with oil (35:14) echoes Gen 28:18. Jubilees 31:1 names it the vow on the day he fled Esau; Jasher 36:1 the altar to the One who appeared.
--   ★ THE NAME REAFFIRMED (THREAD 3): *Thy name shall not be called any more Jacob, but Yashar'el (Israel) shall be thy name* (35:10). The wrestling-name of *as a prince hast thou power with Elohim and with men, and hast prevailed* (Gen 32:28) is now sealed by Elohim Himself in plain appearance — the man who prevailed named for the people he fathers. Jubilees 32:17 keeps it.
--   ★★ EL SHADDAI — A COMPANY OF NATIONS (THREAD 4): *I am El Shaddai (God Almighty): be fruitful and multiply; a nation and a company of nations shall be of thee* (35:11). The SAME El-Shaddai covenant first spoken to Abraham — *I am the El Shaddai... I will make nations of thee, and kings shall come out of thee* (Gen 17:1,6). The *company of nations* is the two-house seed: Ephraim, of whom *his seed shall become a multitude of nations* (Gen 48:19) — the northern house scattered and to be gathered, *the stick of Joseph... and the stick of Yahudah... one stick* (Ezek 37:19), *they shall be no more two nations* (Ezek 37:22), *He that scattered Yashar'el will gather him* (Jer 31:10). Bound per the brief. Read through Red Line #2: never replacement, never a new people; both branches are Yashar'el.
--   ★ RACHEL TO BETHLEHEM (THREAD 5): *Rachel died, and was buried in the way to Ephrath, which is Beth-lehem* (35:19); the son *Ben-oni* (son of my sorrow) → *Benjamin* (son of the right hand). The Bethlehem note reaches forward: *thou, Beth-lehem Ephratah... out of thee shall he come forth... ruler in Yashar'el* (Micah 5:2), and Rachel's grave on that road becomes the weeping-Rachel of *A voice was heard in Ramah... Rahel weeping for her children* (Jer 31:15), fulfilled at *Rachel weeping for her children... because they are not* (Matt 2:18). Jubilees 32:33-34 and Jasher 36:10-12 keep the death and the names.
--   ★ THE SCEPTRE AND THE PRIESTHOOD (THREAD 6): the twelve sons numbered (35:22-26), Reuben's defilement (35:22) costing him the birthright. Jasher 36:15 makes the transfer explicit — *the birthright was given to Joseph, the kingly office to Judah, and the priesthood to Levi* — the three offices distributed: the firstborn-blessing to the house of Joseph/Ephraim, the kingly sceptre to Yahudah (forward to Gen 49:10 / the Davidic king / Messiah), the priesthood to Levi. Jubilees 31:13,18 carries Isaac's blessing of Levi (to serve in His sanctuary) and Yahudah (in you be found the salvation of Yashar'el).
--   EXTRAS: Jubilees 31-32 carry the Bethel return verse-for-verse (clean parse) — the purge (31:1-2), Isaac's blessing of Levi and Yahudah (31:13-18), the tithe and priesthood at Bethel (32:1-9), the name reaffirmation (32:17), the El-Shaddai covenant (32:18-19), Benjamin and Rachel's death at Ephrath/Bethlehem (32:33-34). Jubilees DOUBLE-WRITTEN 'jubilees','jubilees'. Jasher 36 carries the return (36:1-3), the name Israel (36:8), Rachel's death/Benjamin/Bethlehem (36:10-12), and the three-office transfer (36:15). Jasher DOUBLE-WRITTEN 'jasher','jasher'. Jasher 36 places Isaac's death later (not in this chapter), so no extras member for v.27-29.
--   VERSES WITH NO ADD: v.8 (Deborah's death, narrative), v.13-15 (the pillar — folded to THREAD 2 prose), v.21 (the tower of Edar, narrative), v.27-29 (Isaac's death and burial — a closing patriarch-death notice; the Esau-Jacob reconciliation at the grave is a narrative coda, not a framework verse-type in this pack).

CREATE TEMP VIEW _s301_ge35_lookup AS
SELECT e.slug AS edition_slug, b.slug AS book_slug, c.chapter_number, v.verse_number, v.id AS verse_id
  FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON v.chapter_id=c.id JOIN books b ON c.book_id=b.id
  JOIN editions e ON b.edition_id=e.id
 WHERE e.slug IN ('canon','enoch','jubilees','jasher','apocrypha','apocrypha-charles-vol1','pseudepigrapha','adam-eve-conflict','apocalypse-of-abraham','ascension-isaiah','sonnini-acts-29');

INSERT INTO cross_references (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source, note, tier_required)
SELECT sv.verse_id, tv.verse_id, 'manual', i.note, i.tier::content_tier
  FROM (VALUES
    -- THREAD 1: Put away the strange gods, and be clean (cleanse, come out, keep from idols)
    ('canon','genesis',35,2,'canon','2-corinthians',7,1,'free',
      E'*Having therefore these promises, dearly beloved, let us cleanse ourselves from all filthiness of the flesh and spirit, perfecting holiness in the fear of Elohim (God)* (2 Corinthians 7:1). When Jacob commands his house *Put away the strange gods that are among you, and be clean, and change your garments* (Genesis 35:2), it is this same purge before the altar — *let us cleanse ourselves from all filthiness... perfecting holiness*. The strange gods cast off and the garments changed are the body made clean to go up and worship; covenant separation, never a new ethic.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,2,'canon','2-corinthians',6,17,'free',
      E'*Wherefore come out from among them, and be ye separate, saith Yahuah (Lord), and touch not the unclean thing; and I will receive you* (2 Corinthians 6:17). The word *Put away the strange gods... and be clean* (Genesis 35:2) is the same call to separation — *come out from among them, and be ye separate... touch not the unclean thing*. The household that buries its idols is the people set apart unto Yahuah; the gods of the nations have no place among the seed He receives.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,2,'canon','1-john',5,21,'free',
      E'*Little children, keep yourselves from idols. Amen.* (1 John 5:21). The whole of Jacob''s command — *Put away the strange gods that are among you* (Genesis 35:2) — is gathered into the last word of the letter: *keep yourselves from idols*. The teraphim and the earrings buried under the oak are the strange gods the covenant people must never carry; the charge stands from Bethel to the end of the Scriptures.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,4,'canon','genesis',31,19,'free',
      E'*And Laban went to shear his sheep: and Rachel had stolen the images that were her father''s* (Genesis 31:19). The strange gods given up at Bethel — *they gave unto Jacob all the strange gods which were in their hand, and all their earrings... and Jacob hid them under the oak* (Genesis 35:4) — include the very *images* Rachel had stolen from Laban. The teraphim carried out of Padan-aram are now buried under the oak by Shechem; the idol smuggled into the house is purged before the household goes up to the altar.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,2,'jubilees','jubilees',31,1,'extras',
      E'*And on the new moon of the month Jacob spake to all the people of his house, saying: "Purify yourselves and change your garments, and let us arise and go up to Bethel, where I vowed a vow to Him on the day when I fled from the face of Esau my brother, because He has been with me and brought me into this land in peace, and put you away the strange gods that are among you."* (Jubilees 31:1). The restored witness keeps the command whole — *Purify yourselves and change your garments... put you away the strange gods that are among you* — matching *Put away the strange gods that are among you, and be clean, and change your garments* (Genesis 35:2), and binds it to the vow now to be paid.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,4,'jubilees','jubilees',31,2,'extras',
      E'*And they gave up the strange gods and that which was in their ears and which was on their necks, and the idols which Rachel stole from Laban her brother she gave wholly to Jacob. And he burnt and brake them to pieces and destroyed them, and hid them under an oak which is in the land of Shechem* (Jubilees 31:2). The restored witness names what Genesis holds — *they gave unto Jacob all the strange gods... and all their earrings... and Jacob hid them under the oak which was by Shechem* (Genesis 35:4) — and tells plainly that *the idols which Rachel stole from Laban* were among them, burnt and broken before they are buried.'),

    -- THREAD 2: Go up to Beth-el — the vow kept, El-beth-el
    ('canon','genesis',35,1,'canon','genesis',28,20,'free',
      E'*And Jacob vowed a vow, saying, If Elohim (God) will be with me, and will keep me in this way that I go, and will give me bread to eat, and raiment to put on* (Genesis 28:20). The call *Arise, go up to Beth-el, and dwell there: and make there an altar unto Elohim (God), that appeared unto thee when thou fleddest from the face of Esau* (Genesis 35:1) brings Jacob back to pay this very vow — the promise sworn at the stone-pillow now to be honoured at the altar. What he vowed when he fled, he returns to keep when he is brought home in peace.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,7,'canon','genesis',28,21,'free',
      E'*So that I come again to my father''s house in peace; then shall Yahuah (LORD) be my Elohim (God)* (Genesis 28:21). When Jacob *built there an altar, and called the place El-beth-el: because there Elohim (God) appeared unto him, when he fled from the face of his brother* (Genesis 35:7), the condition of the vow is met — he is come again in peace, and now *Yahuah be my Elohim* is sealed in the name El-beth-el, the God of the house of God. The God who met the fleeing man is now the God of the returning man''s altar.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,1,'jubilees','jubilees',31,1,'extras',
      E'*And on the new moon of the month Jacob spake to all the people of his house, saying: "Purify yourselves and change your garments, and let us arise and go up to Bethel, where I vowed a vow to Him on the day when I fled from the face of Esau my brother, because He has been with me and brought me into this land in peace..."* (Jubilees 31:1). The restored witness names the reason for the going up — *to Bethel, where I vowed a vow to Him on the day when I fled* — the same vow-keeping behind *Arise, go up to Beth-el... make there an altar... that appeared unto thee when thou fleddest from the face of Esau* (Genesis 35:1).'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,1,'jasher','jasher',36,1,'extras',
      E'*At that time Yahuah (the Lord) appeared to Jacob saying, Arise, go to Bethel and remain there, and make there an altar to Yahuah (the Lord) who appears to you, who delivered you and your sons from affliction* (Jasher 36:1). The extended witness carries the call whole — *Arise, go to Bethel and remain there, and make there an altar* — matching *Arise, go up to Beth-el, and dwell there: and make there an altar* (Genesis 35:1), naming Yahuah as the One who delivered him in his distress.'),

    -- THREAD 3: Thy name shall be Yashar'el — reaffirmed by Elohim
    ('canon','genesis',35,10,'canon','genesis',32,28,'free',
      E'*And he said, Thy name shall be called no more Jacob, but Yashar''el (Israel): for as a prince hast thou power with Elohim (God) and with men, and hast prevailed* (Genesis 32:28). The new name given at the wrestling by the Jabbok is now sealed in open appearance — *Thy name shall not be called any more Jacob, but Yashar''el (Israel) shall be thy name* (Genesis 35:10). What the man who wrestled won in the night, Elohim Himself confirms by day: the prince who *hast power with Elohim... and hast prevailed* is named for the people he will father.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,10,'jubilees','jubilees',32,17,'extras',
      E'*And Yahuah (God) appeared to him by night and blessed him and said to him: "Your name shall not be called Jacob, but Yashar''el (Israel) shall they name your name."* (Jubilees 32:17). The restored witness keeps the reaffirmation entire — *Your name shall not be called Jacob, but Yashar''el shall they name your name* — matching *Thy name shall not be called any more Jacob, but Yashar''el (Israel) shall be thy name* (Genesis 35:10), the wrestling-name confirmed straight from Yahuah''s mouth.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,10,'jasher','jasher',36,8,'extras',
      E'*And Jacob was a hundred years old when Yahuah (the Lord) appeared to him, and blessed him and called his name Israel, and Rachel the wife of Jacob conceived in those days* (Jasher 36:8). The extended witness joins the appearing, the blessing, and the naming — *Yahuah appeared to him, and blessed him and called his name Israel* — the same seal as *Elohim appeared unto Jacob again... and Elohim said unto him... Yashar''el (Israel) shall be thy name* (Genesis 35:9-10).'),

    -- THREAD 4 (★★): I am El Shaddai — a company of nations (the two-house seed weave)
    ('canon','genesis',35,11,'canon','genesis',17,1,'free',
      E'*And when Abram was ninety years old and nine, Yahuah (LORD) appeared to Abram, and said unto him, I am the El Shaddai (Almighty God); walk before me, and be thou perfect* (Genesis 17:1). The covenant renewed to Jacob — *I am El Shaddai (God Almighty): be fruitful and multiply; a nation and a company of nations shall be of thee* (Genesis 35:11) — is the SAME El-Shaddai promise first spoken to Abraham. The God who named Himself Almighty to the grandfather names Himself so to the grandson; the one covenant runs unbroken down the paternal line.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,11,'canon','genesis',17,6,'free',
      E'*And I will make thee exceeding fruitful, and I will make nations of thee, and kings shall come out of thee* (Genesis 17:6). The word to Jacob — *be fruitful and multiply; a nation and a company of nations shall be of thee, and kings shall come out of thy loins* (Genesis 35:11) — repeats the El-Shaddai grant verse-for-verse: the fruitfulness, the *nations*, the *kings*. The promise of the throne handed from Abraham to Jacob, the kingly seed already sworn before ever a king arose.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,11,'canon','genesis',48,19,'free',
      E'*And his father refused, and said, I know it, my son, I know it: he also shall become a people, and he also shall be great: but truly his younger brother shall be greater than he, and his seed shall become a multitude of nations* (Genesis 48:19). The *company of nations* promised at Bethel — *a nation and a company of nations shall be of thee* (Genesis 35:11) — finds its name in Ephraim, of whom *his seed shall become a multitude of nations*. The multitude-of-nations is the northern house of Joseph, the fulness of the Gentiles that is itself the scattered seed of Yashar''el.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,11,'canon','ezekiel',37,19,'extras',
      E'*Say unto them, Thus saith Adonai Yahuah (the Lord GOD); Behold, I will take the stick of Joseph, which is in the hand of Ephraim, and the tribes of Yashar''el (Israel) his fellows, and will put them with him, even with the stick of Yahudah (Judah), and make them one stick, and they shall be one in mine hand* (Ezekiel 37:19). The *company of nations* of the Bethel covenant (Genesis 35:11) is the two-house people: the stick of Joseph/Ephraim and the stick of Yahudah, scattered apart and to be made *one stick... one in mine hand*. The multitude promised to Jacob is gathered, not replaced.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,11,'canon','ezekiel',37,22,'extras',
      E'*And I will make them one nation in the land upon the mountains of Yashar''el (Israel); and one king shall be king to them all: and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all* (Ezekiel 37:22). The *nation and a company of nations* of Genesis 35:11 ends not in two divided kingdoms but in *one nation... one king*: the houses of Yahudah and Ephraim made whole again on the mountains of Yashar''el. The Bethel promise of multitude is the promise of an ingathered, undivided people.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,11,'canon','jeremiah',31,10,'extras',
      E'*Hear the word of Yahuah (LORD), O ye nations, and declare it in the isles afar off, and say, He that scattered Yashar''el (Israel) will gather him, and keep him, as a shepherd doth his flock* (Jeremiah 31:10). The *company of nations* sworn at Bethel (Genesis 35:11) is scattered *in the isles afar off* and then regathered: *He that scattered Yashar''el will gather him*. The God who made Jacob a multitude of nations is the Shepherd who will gather that multitude home — never a new flock, but His own scattered sheep kept and brought back.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,12,'jubilees','jubilees',32,18,'extras',
      E'*And He said to him again: "I am Yahuah (God) who created the heaven and the earth, and I shall increase you and multiply you exceedingly, and kings will come forth from you, and they will judge everywhere wherever the foot of the sons of men has trodden."* (Jubilees 32:18). The restored witness keeps the El-Shaddai covenant — *I shall increase you and multiply you exceedingly, and kings will come forth from you* — alongside *I am El Shaddai... be fruitful and multiply... and kings shall come out of thy loins* (Genesis 35:11), and *the land which I gave Abraham and Isaac, to thee I will give it* (Genesis 35:12), the seed and the land sworn together.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,12,'jubilees','jubilees',32,19,'extras',
      E'*And I shall give to your seed all the earth which is under heaven, and they will judge all the nations according to their desires, and after that they will get possession of the whole earth and inherit it for ever* (Jubilees 32:19). The land-grant of Bethel — *the land which I gave Abraham and Isaac, to thee I will give it, and to thy seed after thee* (Genesis 35:12) — is carried in the restored witness to its fulness: *I shall give to your seed all the earth... and inherit it for ever*. The land promised to the fathers widens to the whole earth inherited by the gathered seed.'),

    -- THREAD 5: Rachel buried on the way to Bethlehem (Ben-oni/Benjamin; weeping Rachel)
    ('canon','genesis',35,19,'canon','micah',5,2,'free',
      E'*But thou, Beth-lehem Ephratah, though thou be little among the thousands of Yahudah (Judah), yet out of thee shall he come forth unto me that is to be ruler in Yashar''el (Israel); whose goings forth have been from of old, from everlasting* (Micah 5:2). Rachel is *buried in the way to Ephrath, which is Beth-lehem* (Genesis 35:19) — the little town where the prophet says the eternal Ruler will come forth. The grave on the Bethlehem road marks the very place that will birth the One whose *goings forth have been... from everlasting*.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,19,'canon','jeremiah',31,15,'free',
      E'*Thus saith Yahuah (LORD); A voice was heard in Ramah, lamentation, and bitter weeping; Rahel weeping for her children refused to be comforted for her children, because they were not* (Jeremiah 31:15). Rachel, buried *in the way to Ephrath, which is Beth-lehem* (Genesis 35:19), becomes the prophet''s figure of the mother of Yashar''el weeping over the scattered and the slain — *Rahel weeping for her children... because they were not*. The grave by the road becomes the lament for the exiled seed, set in the very chapter that promises their ingathering.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,19,'canon','matthew',2,18,'free',
      E'*In Rama was there a voice heard, lamentation, and weeping, and great mourning, Rachel weeping for her children, and would not be comforted, because they are not* (Matthew 2:18). The weeping foretold over Rachel''s Bethlehem grave (Genesis 35:19; Jeremiah 31:15) is named fulfilled when the children of Beth-lehem are slain — *Rachel weeping for her children... because they are not*. The mother buried on that road still weeps over the town where the Ruler is born; sorrow and promise meet at Ephrath.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,18,'jubilees','jubilees',32,33,'extras',
      E'*And Rachel bare a son in the night, and called his name "Son of my sorrow"; for she suffered in giving him birth: but his father called his name Benjamin, on the eleventh of the eighth month in the first of the sixth week of this jubilee* (Jubilees 32:33). The restored witness keeps both names — *"Son of my sorrow"... but his father called his name Benjamin* — matching *as her soul was in departing... she called his name Ben-oni: but his father called him Benjamin* (Genesis 35:18): the dying mother''s sorrow turned by the father into the son of the right hand.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,19,'jasher','jasher',36,11,'extras',
      E'*And Jacob buried her in the way to Ephrath, which is Bethlehem, and he set a pillar upon her grave, which is there to this day; and the days of Rachel were forty-five years and she died* (Jasher 36:11). The extended witness carries the burial whole — *buried her in the way to Ephrath, which is Bethlehem, and he set a pillar upon her grave* — matching *Rachel died, and was buried in the way to Ephrath, which is Beth-lehem. And Jacob set a pillar upon her grave* (Genesis 35:19-20).'),

    -- THREAD 6: The twelve sons — the sceptre and the priesthood
    ('canon','genesis',35,23,'jasher','jasher',36,15,'extras',
      E'*At that time the portion of birthright, together with the kingly and priestly offices, was removed from the sons of Reuben, for he had profaned his father''s bed, and the birthright was given to Joseph, the kingly office to Judah, and the priesthood to Levi, because Reuben had defiled his father''s bed* (Jasher 36:15). The twelve sons are numbered with Reuben first — *Reuben, Jacob''s firstborn* (Genesis 35:23) — but his defilement (Genesis 35:22) forfeits the firstborn''s portion: the extended witness names the threefold transfer — *the birthright... to Joseph, the kingly office to Judah, and the priesthood to Levi* — the offices that will shape the whole nation.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,23,'jubilees','jubilees',31,18,'extras',
      E'*And to Yahudah (Judah) he said: May Yahuah (God) give you strength and power To tread down all that hate you; A prince shall you be, you and one of your sons, over the sons of Jacob... In you shall be the help of Jacob, And in you be found the salvation of Yashar''el (Israel)* (Jubilees 31:18). Among the twelve sons numbered at Bethel — *the sons of Leah; Reuben, Jacob''s firstborn, and Simeon, and Levi, and Yahudah (Judah)* (Genesis 35:23) — the kingly office falls to Yahudah, and the restored witness sings it: *A prince shall you be... In you be found the salvation of Yashar''el*. The sceptre that goes to Judah carries the seed-promise toward the King to come.'),
    ('canon','genesis',35,23,'jubilees','jubilees',31,13,'extras',
      E'*And he turned to Levi first, and began to bless him first, and said to him: "May the Elohim (God) of all... bless you and your children throughout all the ages... and cause you and your seed, from among all flesh, to approach Him to serve in His sanctuary as the angels of the presence and as the holy ones."* (Jubilees 31:13). Of the twelve sons (Genesis 35:23), the priesthood falls to Levi, and the restored witness gives Isaac''s blessing upon him — *to approach Him to serve in His sanctuary*. The tribe set apart to draw near is marked here at Bethel, the priestly office settled among the sons of Jacob.')
  ) AS i(src_edition,src_slug,src_ch,src_v,tgt_edition,tgt_slug,tgt_ch,tgt_v,tier,note)
  JOIN _s301_ge35_lookup sv ON sv.edition_slug=i.src_edition AND sv.book_slug=i.src_slug AND sv.chapter_number=i.src_ch AND sv.verse_number=i.src_v
  JOIN _s301_ge35_lookup tv ON tv.edition_slug=i.tgt_edition AND tv.book_slug=i.tgt_slug AND tv.chapter_number=i.tgt_ch AND tv.verse_number=i.tgt_v
 WHERE sv.verse_id <> tv.verse_id
ON CONFLICT (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 1
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'genesis-35-put-away-the-strange-gods-and-be-clean',
       E'Put away the strange gods, and be clean',
       E'Before the household can go up to the altar, it must be purged. *Then Jacob said unto his household, and to all that were with him, Put away the strange gods that are among you, and be clean, and change your garments* (Genesis 35:2) — and they obey: *they gave unto Jacob all the strange gods which were in their hand, and all their earrings which were in their ears; and Jacob hid them under the oak which was by Shechem* (Genesis 35:4). Among them are the very teraphim Rachel carried out of Padan-aram — *Rachel had stolen the images that were her father''s* (Genesis 31:19) — the idol smuggled into the house now buried before the journey to Bethel. The restored witness tells it plainly: *Purify yourselves and change your garments... put you away the strange gods that are among you* (Jubilees 31:1), and *the idols which Rachel stole from Laban... he burnt and brake them to pieces and destroyed them, and hid them under an oak which is in the land of Shechem* (Jubilees 31:2). And the same command runs forward to the assembly of the covenant: *let us cleanse ourselves from all filthiness of the flesh and spirit, perfecting holiness in the fear of Elohim (God)* (2 Corinthians 7:1); *come out from among them, and be ye separate, saith Yahuah (Lord), and touch not the unclean thing* (2 Corinthians 6:17); and the last word of the elder''s letter, *Little children, keep yourselves from idols. Amen.* (1 John 5:21). The strange gods cast off and the garments changed are not a passing rite but the abiding shape of a people set apart — holiness is covenant-keeping, the household made clean to worship.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'extras', 20850
  FROM _s301_ge35_lookup sv, _s301_ge35_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='genesis' AND sv.chapter_number=35 AND sv.verse_number=2
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='genesis' AND ev.chapter_number=35 AND ev.verse_number=4
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 2
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'genesis-35-go-up-to-bethel-the-vow-kept-el-bethel',
       E'Go up to Beth-el — the vow kept, El-beth-el',
       E'*And Elohim (God) said unto Jacob, Arise, go up to Beth-el, and dwell there: and make there an altar unto Elohim (God), that appeared unto thee when thou fleddest from the face of Esau thy brother* (Genesis 35:1). This is a summons to pay a debt. Years before, fleeing with nothing but a stone for a pillow, Jacob had sworn: *And Jacob vowed a vow, saying, If Elohim (God) will be with me, and will keep me in this way that I go, and will give me bread to eat, and raiment to put on, So that I come again to my father''s house in peace; then shall Yahuah (LORD) be my Elohim (God)* (Genesis 28:20-21). Now he is come again in peace, with wives, children, and flocks, and the time to keep the vow has come. *And he built there an altar, and called the place El-beth-el: because there Elohim (God) appeared unto him, when he fled from the face of his brother* (Genesis 35:7) — El-beth-el, the God of the house of God. He sets up the pillar again and pours oil upon it as at the first (Genesis 35:14), and the safe journey is guarded: *the terror of Elohim (God) was upon the cities that were round about them* (Genesis 35:5). The restored witnesses keep it: *let us arise and go up to Bethel, where I vowed a vow to Him on the day when I fled from the face of Esau my brother* (Jubilees 31:1), and *Arise, go to Bethel and remain there, and make there an altar to Yahuah (the Lord) who appears to you, who delivered you and your sons from affliction* (Jasher 36:1). The God who met the fleeing man at the stone is the God of the returning man''s altar; the vow sworn in fear is kept in peace.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'extras', 20853
  FROM _s301_ge35_lookup sv, _s301_ge35_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='genesis' AND sv.chapter_number=35 AND sv.verse_number=1
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='genesis' AND ev.chapter_number=35 AND ev.verse_number=7
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 3
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'genesis-35-thy-name-shall-be-yasharel-reaffirmed',
       E'Thy name shall be Yashar''el — reaffirmed by Elohim',
       E'*And Elohim (God) appeared unto Jacob again, when he came out of Padan-aram, and blessed him. And Elohim (God) said unto him, Thy name is Jacob: thy name shall not be called any more Jacob, but Yashar''el (Israel) shall be thy name: and he called his name Yashar''el (Israel)* (Genesis 35:9-10). The name was first wrenched from the dark at the Jabbok, won in the wrestling: *Thy name shall be called no more Jacob, but Yashar''el (Israel): for as a prince hast thou power with Elohim (God) and with men, and hast prevailed* (Genesis 32:28). What the night-struggle granted, the open appearing of Elohim now seals — no longer the supplanter (Jacob, the heel-holder) but Yashar''el, the prince who prevailed, named for the people he will father. The restored witness keeps the reaffirmation: *And Yahuah (God) appeared to him by night and blessed him and said to him: "Your name shall not be called Jacob, but Yashar''el (Israel) shall they name your name"* (Jubilees 32:17), and the extended witness joins appearing, blessing, and naming in one breath: *Yahuah (the Lord) appeared to him, and blessed him and called his name Israel* (Jasher 36:8). The name of the man becomes the name of the nation; the seed will be called by the name of the one who held on until the blessing came.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'extras', 20856
  FROM _s301_ge35_lookup sv, _s301_ge35_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='genesis' AND sv.chapter_number=35 AND sv.verse_number=9
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='genesis' AND ev.chapter_number=35 AND ev.verse_number=10
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 4 (★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'genesis-35-i-am-el-shaddai-a-company-of-nations',
       E'I am El Shaddai — a company of nations (the two-house seed)',
       E'*And Elohim (God) said unto him, I am El Shaddai (God Almighty): be fruitful and multiply; a nation and a company of nations shall be of thee, and kings shall come out of thy loins; And the land which I gave Abraham and Isaac, to thee I will give it, and to thy seed after thee will I give the land* (Genesis 35:11-12). This is the Abrahamic covenant renewed in Jacob, word for word from the grandfather: *I am the El Shaddai (Almighty God)... I will make thee exceeding fruitful, and I will make nations of thee, and kings shall come out of thee* (Genesis 17:1,6). The seed and the land sworn together, the kings foretold before any king arose. But hear the strange phrase: *a company of nations*. It is no idle plural. It is fulfilled in Ephraim, of whom Jacob himself will prophesy, *his seed shall become a multitude of nations* (Genesis 48:19) — the northern house of Joseph, scattered through the nations and grown wild, yet never cast off. For the same God who made Jacob a multitude swears to gather that multitude home: *Behold, I will take the stick of Joseph, which is in the hand of Ephraim... even with the stick of Yahudah (Judah), and make them one stick, and they shall be one in mine hand* (Ezekiel 37:19); *they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all* (Ezekiel 37:22); *He that scattered Yashar''el (Israel) will gather him, and keep him, as a shepherd doth his flock* (Jeremiah 31:10). The company of nations is the two-house people — Yahudah and Ephraim — divided for a season and made one again, never replaced by a new people, never grafted in by confession apart from the covenant, but the very seed of Jacob gathered from the isles afar off. The restored witness keeps the covenant and widens the land: *I am Yahuah (God) who created the heaven and the earth, and I shall increase you and multiply you exceedingly, and kings will come forth from you* (Jubilees 32:18), *And I shall give to your seed all the earth which is under heaven... and inherit it for ever* (Jubilees 32:19). What is sworn at Bethel reaches to the gathering of all the seed.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'extras', 20859
  FROM _s301_ge35_lookup sv, _s301_ge35_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='genesis' AND sv.chapter_number=35 AND sv.verse_number=11
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='genesis' AND ev.chapter_number=35 AND ev.verse_number=12
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 5
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'genesis-35-rachel-buried-on-the-way-to-bethlehem',
       E'Rachel buried on the way to Beth-lehem — Ben-oni, the son of the right hand',
       E'The journey from Bethel turns to grief. *And they journeyed from Beth-el; and there was but a little way to come to Ephrath: and Rachel travailed, and she had hard labour* (Genesis 35:16). The midwife comforts her — *Fear not; thou shalt have this son also* (Genesis 35:17) — but the birth costs her life: *as her soul was in departing, (for she died) that she called his name Ben-oni: but his father called him Benjamin* (Genesis 35:18). Son of my sorrow, the dying mother names him; son of the right hand, the father renames him — grief turned to honour. *And Rachel died, and was buried in the way to Ephrath, which is Beth-lehem. And Jacob set a pillar upon her grave* (Genesis 35:19-20). That little town is no accident. *But thou, Beth-lehem Ephratah, though thou be little among the thousands of Yahudah (Judah), yet out of thee shall he come forth unto me that is to be ruler in Yashar''el (Israel); whose goings forth have been from of old, from everlasting* (Micah 5:2) — the grave on the Bethlehem road marks the very place that will birth the eternal Ruler. And Rachel''s weeping does not end at her grave: *A voice was heard in Ramah, lamentation, and bitter weeping; Rahel weeping for her children refused to be comforted for her children, because they were not* (Jeremiah 31:15) — the mother of Yashar''el made the figure of every exile and every slain child, set in the very chapter that promises the ingathering. It is named fulfilled when the children of Bethlehem are slain: *In Rama was there a voice heard... Rachel weeping for her children, and would not be comforted, because they are not* (Matthew 2:18). The restored witnesses keep the names and the place: *she... called his name "Son of my sorrow"... but his father called his name Benjamin* (Jubilees 32:33), and *Jacob buried her in the way to Ephrath, which is Bethlehem, and he set a pillar upon her grave* (Jasher 36:11). Sorrow and promise meet at Ephrath: the grave of the beloved wife, the birthplace of the King.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'extras', 20862
  FROM _s301_ge35_lookup sv, _s301_ge35_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='genesis' AND sv.chapter_number=35 AND sv.verse_number=16
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='genesis' AND ev.chapter_number=35 AND ev.verse_number=20
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 6
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'genesis-35-the-twelve-sons-the-sceptre-and-the-priesthood',
       E'The twelve sons — the sceptre and the priesthood',
       E'The chapter numbers the whole house: *Now the sons of Jacob were twelve* (Genesis 35:22), set out by their mothers — *The sons of Leah; Reuben, Jacob''s firstborn, and Simeon, and Levi, and Yahudah (Judah), and Issachar, and Zebulun* (Genesis 35:23), then the sons of Rachel, of Bilhah, of Zilpah (Genesis 35:24-26). But the firstborn has fallen: *Reuben went and lay with Bilhah his father''s concubine: and Yashar''el (Israel) heard it* (Genesis 35:22), and the defilement of the father''s bed costs him the firstborn''s portion. The extended witness names the threefold transfer that will shape the nation: *the portion of birthright, together with the kingly and priestly offices, was removed from the sons of Reuben... and the birthright was given to Joseph, the kingly office to Judah, and the priesthood to Levi* (Jasher 36:15). The double-portion of the firstborn passes to the house of Joseph; the kingly sceptre to Yahudah — *A prince shall you be... In you be found the salvation of Yashar''el (Israel)* (Jubilees 31:18), the line that runs to the throne of David and beyond; and the priesthood to Levi, the tribe set apart to draw near — *cause you and your seed, from among all flesh, to approach Him to serve in His sanctuary* (Jubilees 31:13). At Bethel the offices are settled: the firstborn-blessing, the crown, and the altar distributed among the sons of Jacob, the architecture of the covenant people laid down in the twelve.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'extras', 20865
  FROM _s301_ge35_lookup sv, _s301_ge35_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='genesis' AND sv.chapter_number=35 AND sv.verse_number=22
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='genesis' AND ev.chapter_number=35 AND ev.verse_number=26
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

